From ad2ef8ba6f7a292b40435d13472477f543b8baf9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aryan Hamedani <aryn.hmd@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:39:28 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] feat(capture): add exclusive sessions

With exclusive_session (--exclusive-session), the headless output is off
between sessions. When a client connects it is turned on, the other outputs
are turned off, and Hyprland moves every workspace and window to it, keeping
the workspace that was in front. On disconnect the other outputs come back
with their exact settings before the headless output goes off, so Hyprland
always keeps an output. Config reloads re-apply this state, and a restart
after an unclean exit reloads Hyprland's config to bring the outputs back.

The virtual pointer is bound again when the headless output returns, since
turning it off destroys its wl_output.

Also: a late initial-size request no longer overrides a DisplayControl layout
from the same session (it restarted capture and dropped clients that connect
on a portrait monitor), and Lua monitor rules carry disabled = false like
their legacy form, so they turn a disabled output back on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
